{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:45:32.324632Z","id":"de7b2119a2f85cc687342ec267c464b66eb2547335606bb5592f2af76c641b7f","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The same record as d44e91f0 at crates/clax-http/src/audit.rs:333, kept: this head is a re-anchor of it made on a branch while main moved it there","supersedes":"8ca5839efcfee4c03e8834d1a2c21c5c8a0367be4044bb3985b7576eac971cfe","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:45:32.345215Z","id":"9c8c2c6a39be8aae93fbb66a39aae6c7e567d25ad868541c5dfc537484bfde70","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The same record as 0a1a0d4b at crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:28, kept: this head is a re-anchor of it made on a branch while main moved it there","supersedes":"200d4d60fab2ffe95e394bc9fec4d4e90f3b6be748788470629851d0f66cf5c1","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:45:32.365825Z","id":"5dc64835faa378133d30df87595201c8534485d77e04617c3533b6e9ed955754","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The same record as c77c0394 at crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:651, kept: this head is a re-anchor of it made on a branch while main moved it there","supersedes":"b38524341e82a3ea019df5cbc1b1bbfb67fc80903d6680738695fe760274d0de","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/viewer.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:45:32.407341Z","id":"1775a65e90531ff18cd9c0f2f4dace1bc50ea68ca8f7594b90a3fda54db0545c","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The same record as 15bc103c at crates/clax-http/src/viewer.rs:119, kept: this head is a re-anchor of it made on a branch while main moved it there","supersedes":"29e9b7574a064936b94afb460ed2ed08221353af4802440403d1377126095bdc","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:50:52.382230Z","id":"924f246c3d11dfd9cdf02556bed14c4a9b5b18118a7d4c6c868b5a919429fec2","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:565-591, record 4585fb7a.\n\nThe keyed address is an HMAC of <aid>/<tid> (clip_key), not a hash of the PNG: a thread's clip is written once and never changes for that (artifact, thread) pair (a move to another artifact makes a new pair, crates/clax-core/src/store/site.rs put_clip), so the address is immutable without reading every clip to hash it for a listing. Clips stay stored once per thread (ContentStore::put_clip). The hosted shell still loads clip_url (GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/threads/<tid>/clip, credentialed, Cache-Control private, max-age=3600); thread views carry clip_link only for agents (VisFor::of in crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs). Pointing the shell's <img> at the keyed address would make one cacheable URL for both, and needs browser verification of the hosted shell.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:4728cf5c20cb059a7675fcf56d04b297532ab930","span":{"start":{"line":562},"end":{"line":588},"content_hash":"7680213e958ae6c8505afa1feb64c74fc558f0d4e477611011fe04da896cc7db"},"summary":"Key a clip's address by its content hash, and have the hosted shell load clips from it","tags":["hosted","revisit:hosted shell clip loads show in the time-to-usable budget, or a clip's bytes may change for its thread","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:19:13.428782Z","id":"f8e0cbe9bb0bc6ee4aa0f33f791f023027dce1f32d8e53bfe459a35fa3320e80","body":{"detail":"5274dba44 added hosted mode (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:31-38 now describes it): there the clax_viewer cookie counts for nothing and a browser is the viewer its session signs in as, a person's or a guest's. crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs Limits (lines 150-215, per client address, on an injected clock) rate-limit setup, sign-in, naming a guest (Attempt::Guest: 5 at once, one back per 120 s), device sign-in, git tokens and GitHub sign-up; no thread, comment, send or db document route takes an attempt (Hosted::attempt, line 438, is called only for those kinds). A guest's comments reach agents only once the owner approves them, but they are stored without limit. The decision this record asks for now covers a hosted daemon's guests as well as LAN viewers.","kind":"comment","references":"0a1a0d4b04504252c8f9703038c055b7e0ee47f052ebc29bf8a1458c77a32cd3","summary":"Changed since recorded: a hosted daemon's guests, from the internet, are viewers too, and their writes have no rate limit either","tags":["security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:19:56.296519Z","id":"b6c59ca7c80bb8e2ca7d72d2dad8d9491aae5b037475ff67a0d3b6fb767502c3","body":{"detail":"clax_http::surface::signals sets Signals.artifact_id to the gated page, else the last delivery's artifact, so clax_core::surface::place_of (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs) places a suggestion whose delivery is older than the last prompt on that artifact rather than on nothing. Not taken: preferring the delivery's artifact over the page, or leaving artifact_id as the page alone (the delivery then places nothing once a prompt is newer).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"9dbf23e2cd1b2790cf84c21e6f34061d651c1c6f1d92cfc4ef7b215cf572b78d"},"summary":"With no page, the delivery's artifact stands in as the session's page; a page, when there is one, wins over an older delivery's artifact","tags":["revisit:a session's page and its last delivery's artifact differ and questions land on the wrong one","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:19:56.347241Z","id":"2794ddc94b4a3aad55f2013fd798e3c7d77855cde02549795e0da817838cb6a2","body":{"detail":"signals reads the delivery from Store::session_signals and checks only that the thread is still on its artifact. A person's agent had that thread delivered, so it already knows both IDs, but if the owner narrows its rights afterwards (crates/clax-server/tests/api_where_to_ask.rs a_persons_agent_is_never_shown_a_page_it_may_not_read covers only the page) GET /api/sessions/{id}/where-to-ask still names them in where. Gating would make signals async or take the delivery's readability as an argument.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":75},"end":{"line":94},"content_hash":"1f32acb09dd32893c31459f5d70ffee5aa0ca1deeebf7daaa50f1c37a03dadf4"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the delivery's artifact through Agent::named_artifact in clax_http::surface::page's caller and drop the delivery's place when it fails.","summary":"The last delivery's artifact and thread are not passed through the agent's gate (Agent::named_artifact), unlike the page","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:56:07.718293Z","id":"19828f45103bb56569db35d0908af2cee3eab1f3d1611bc2c184e572c94f131e","body":{"detail":"clax_http::surface::gather sets Signals.artifact_id to the gated page, else the last delivery's artifact, so clax_core::surface::place_of (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs) places a suggestion whose delivery is older than the last prompt on that artifact rather than on nothing. Not taken: preferring the delivery's artifact over the page, or leaving artifact_id as the page alone (the delivery then places nothing once a prompt is newer).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":115},"content_hash":"9dbf23e2cd1b2790cf84c21e6f34061d651c1c6f1d92cfc4ef7b215cf572b78d"},"summary":"With no page, the delivery's artifact stands in as the session's page; a page, when there is one, wins over an older delivery's artifact","supersedes":"b6c59ca7c80bb8e2ca7d72d2dad8d9491aae5b037475ff67a0d3b6fb767502c3","tags":["revisit:a session's page and its last delivery's artifact differ and questions land on the wrong one","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
