{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.074763Z","id":"dc442316ca02e3f9a5a1795a6a78fb5bd08fe2f98f466118be094932367fa080","body":{"detail":"clax_http::surface::gather sets Signals.artifact_id to the gated page, else the last delivery's artifact, so clax_core::surface::place_of (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs) places a suggestion whose delivery is older than the last prompt on that artifact rather than on nothing. Not taken: preferring the delivery's artifact over the page, or leaving artifact_id as the page alone (the delivery then places nothing once a prompt is newer).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":124},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"9dbf23e2cd1b2790cf84c21e6f34061d651c1c6f1d92cfc4ef7b215cf572b78d"},"summary":"With no page, the delivery's artifact stands in as the session's page; a page, when there is one, wins over an older delivery's artifact","supersedes":"bc165d9a937d392eff78f7eee7a3b57eb023676226cbe49ca1e626540e975bde","tags":["revisit:a session's page and its last delivery's artifact differ and questions land on the wrong one","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T12:19:34.874336Z","id":"dfb2b94c88eee4da6ce67e07819f0c50bd379ad998386b1f0ace55f13b64fd6a","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs serves a draft's files with content_policy(.., None) and sets no ContentPolicySet, so rewrite_artifact_host appends the lockdown (own files under /c/<id>/, the bridge, /_blob/<id>/, connect-src 'none'). Policies only narrow, and the draft's own files are under /c/<id>/, but no test covers a draft page under the lockdown (web/e2e/drafts.spec.ts runs the base's drafts; check it passes).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"301b95f7aeb38a56eec2f7d801ccf7abd0a3488b0d981ba06a32525771057917"},"summary":"The base's agent draft pages at /c/<id>/draft/... now get the artifact's lockdown policy appended here, beside the policy their route sets","tags":["drafts","security","rebase","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T13:51:39.780794Z","id":"c8a3a59bb761649cd9724607026bc388d5390f4a5ab0f587bc818e9797f96815","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs serves a draft's files with content_policy(.., None) and sets no ContentPolicySet, so rewrite_artifact_host appends the lockdown (own files under /c/<id>/, the bridge, /_blob/<id>/, connect-src 'none'). Policies only narrow, and the draft's own files are under /c/<id>/; web/e2e/drafts.spec.ts passed under just ci after the rebase, but no test asserts a draft page's policy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"100a0b599d3c2773d4a62798a4534806f6dbca1d14d16fc6911ed371eb441ba1"},"summary":"The base's agent draft pages at /c/<id>/draft/... now get the artifact's lockdown policy appended here, beside the policy their route sets","supersedes":"dfb2b94c88eee4da6ce67e07819f0c50bd379ad998386b1f0ace55f13b64fd6a","tags":["drafts","security","rebase","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T13:51:41.217733Z","id":"00771300c3144d42037ee8fe4ce84fb89c41ef01d7e98241bbd76176c8daea85","body":{"detail":"scripts/check-wasm.sh (CI's worker job, not just ci) checks clax-http for wasm32-unknown-unknown; this branch's net.rs and net_cache.rs use reqwest, DNS and the disk, and AppState carries a net field. The check was not run after the rebase onto akesling/clax-artifacts (it runs cargo natively); expect it to need cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\")) gates.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"ecc378603e97b221f84cb5882f62b5e9152ea1c65275c1029b79cf243119213e"},"summary":"net and net_cache (the app pages' fetch through the daemon) are compiled on every target, unchecked for the Worker's wasm32 build","tags":["wasm","rebase","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T14:07:46.730612Z","id":"a4abc538739bceee4ddd11d87833bc5951bc972cf0deabe00c746c9a475e2928","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: net, net_cache, AppState::net and the net routes are native-only. Evidence: CARGO_TARGET_DIR=target/cargo-wasm just check-wasm exits 0 (it failed with 11 errors in crates/clax-http/src/net.rs and net_cache.rs before), and just worker-test exits 0.","supersedes":"00771300c3144d42037ee8fe4ce84fb89c41ef01d7e98241bbd76176c8daea85","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:35:14.558213Z","id":"a901b7b806a523eb647a2a1e62610efbb8b1eb878cdcc583f9bb97589a99235a","body":{"detail":"axum 0.8.9 src/serve/listener.rs:30-37 loops 'match Self::accept(self).await { Ok(tup) => return tup, Err(e) => handle_accept_error(e).await }'. handle_accept_error (:140-158) returns at once when is_connection_error (:160-167: ConnectionRefused, ConnectionAborted, ConnectionReset), else logs 'error!(\"accept error: {e}\")' and runs 'tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_secs(1)).await'. So a listener the OS has reclaimed (iOS may close a suspended app's sockets) costs one error log line a second and never ends serve: the daemon keeps running on a dead socket until its host notices (a failing /healthz) and stops and restarts it. Checked against the axum 0.8.9 source crate_universe fetched (Cargo.lock pins axum 0.8.9).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":453},"end":{"line":457},"content_hash":"8ed331101280a14d1d68691a00f18a00232b6e51e8a7fc0d11160a1249d21299"},"summary":"TunedListener::accept never returns an accept error: axum 0.8.9's Listener for TcpListener retries every one, at once for a per-connection error and after a 1 s sleep for any other","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/jobs_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:19:56.893437Z","id":"4f781e2e1b84fe9b97c37a5b91f5714148146bc9a301acdfa5bd28897f76b556","body":{"detail":"Claimed::Held tells the claimant to wait for jobs_owner with held:false (spec §7.5; routes/jobs.rs claim). The claim does not check that `stream` follows the `jobs` topic. A worker that subscribes to `jobs` after its refused claim misses a release in between and, with no clock, never claims again. The embed test the_queue_owner_is_released_when_its_subscriber_goes (crates/clax-embed/tests/embed.rs) subscribes before it claims, so it does not hit this case.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"de280f97d76a925d392f99a82fc61f0daa0513cdf5af6412b176615053998689"},"suggested_fix":"Before answering Held, subscribe the claimant's stream to `jobs` (Hub::update, as POST /api/stream/{id} does), or refuse a claim whose stream does not follow `jobs` with 400 not_following_jobs; write the order into spec §7.5.","summary":"A claimant refused with owner_held is woken only by held:false on the jobs topic, which nothing makes its stream follow","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/jobs_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:00:13.673382Z","id":"645111610afff4ed286bff971f95c4c6af6033170da9f2274f25e6a5af9aeb75","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed: POST /api/jobs/owner first subscribes the claimant's stream to the jobs topic (as the caller that opened it; 400 no_such_stream otherwise), so a claimant refused owner_held hears the release. Test passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1 (api_jobs::a_claimant_refused_owner_held_hears_the_release, a release before the claimant subscribed); before the fix it timed out waiting for jobs_owner held false.","supersedes":"4f781e2e1b84fe9b97c37a5b91f5714148146bc9a301acdfa5bd28897f76b556","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/jobs_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:08:37.180922Z","id":"e9e3a24f7230bfed15a67cefb97f24ab86f5b94cd58dba944fb7f87dd435098f","body":{"detail":"claim() puts the new claim in the map, then awaits drained() before answering. A second claim from the same stream while the first is still waiting (a client that retries a slow claim, or the first request cancelled) takes the early return at line 174 (c.stream == stream answers c.token at once), so it gets the token while writes admitted under the old claim are still running. enter() then admits the new owner's writes alongside them, which breaks the contract docs/contract.md states for POST /api/jobs/owner ('the new claim answers only once the writes admitted under the old one have ended'). Fix: on the same-stream branch, also await drained(client, &token) and check holds(), or have enter() refuse a token while writes_of_others(client, token) is true, so the guarantee does not depend on how the token was obtained.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":172},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"aea7ee713bfca1532d289bfc871e47ca74d9f75aa2a1ca50aa58a2018e0aa4db"},"summary":"A claim by the claimant's own stream answers its token before the old claim's writes have drained","tags":["jobs-owner","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/jobs_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:08:37.180952Z","id":"be4b2d6bdd39b7760464ffbc69f837c65b51ccdc6bbb174beda31bb91bd839f8","body":{"detail":"require_owner (crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs:70) answers a WriteGuard that the handler holds across s.store_call / store_call_async. On the pool (Exec::Pool, the daemon and the app's embedded core when the content store needs no executor) that call runs the job on a worker thread (crates/clax-store/src/exec.rs call_async, call_on_worker). When the handler future is dropped, the guard drops while the worker's write goes on. That happens when the old owner's process dies and its HTTP connection closes, which is the case the guard exists for, and when the core's close cuts calls in flight. The new claim then answers and its writes race the old write. The rev and if_rev checks still serialise job rows, but the contract's 'none of them lands after it' does not hold. a_new_claim_answers_only_once_the_old_claims_write_has_landed (crates/clax-server/tests/api_jobs.rs) runs on one connection, where the write is awaited inline and is dropped with the handler, so it does not exercise this. Also, drained() waits for as long as the slowest old write (a content write to a stalled remote), holding the claim's HTTP request open with no bound and no answer. Fix: move the guard into the store job's closure or future (drop it where the write ends, on the worker), and test it with a pool store and a request dropped mid-write. Consider answering a claim that has to wait with 409 owner_draining at once, and publishing jobs_owner {held: true} when the drain ends: the claimant's stream already follows jobs (20e1ed98c3fc), no request hangs, and a cancelled claim no longer leaves a claim whose token no answer carried.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"bdbbeef9342019156eb169c6aae94a0325f4dcdd77efd48588cff8b6881bee79"},"summary":"A write's guard lives in the handler, so a cancelled request ends the drain while its store job still runs, and a stuck write holds a new claim with no bound","tags":["jobs-owner","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/jobs_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:13:44.677206Z","id":"b70fd8c564135a51ce6c84afc79e00311689646d7a2c7711807d79a61a79869d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: a claim by the stream that holds the queue answers Claimed::Draining (409 owner_draining) while writes admitted under an older claim run, and enter() admits no write under a draining claim however the token was had. Test api_jobs::a_new_claim_drains_at_once_and_holds_the_queue_once_the_old_write_has_landed (crates/clax-server/tests/api_jobs.rs: a second claim of the stream, one in flight and one after, both 409 owner_draining) fails with the old same-stream branch restored (200 with the token) and passes; jobs_owner::tests::a_new_claim_drains_until_the_old_claims_writes_end checks it at unit level. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all //crates/clax-content-git:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-core:all: all PASSED; //crates/clax-server:integration__1 --test_arg=api_jobs:: --runs_per_test=10: 10 of 10 passed (16 tests each).","supersedes":"e9e3a24f7230bfed15a67cefb97f24ab86f5b94cd58dba944fb7f87dd435098f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/jobs_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:13:44.733011Z","id":"40b77ef5aae7bb748868f66df91a5abbba00a044c5e70cf83d81ee89d87e3f5d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc and 20e1ed98c3fc: a claim that must drain answers 409 owner_draining at once and a task publishes jobs_owner {held: true} when the old writes end (no request waits); every job route moves its WriteGuard into the store job (store_call closure, or the publish step's future), so it ends with the write on the worker thread. docs/contract.md and the spec §7.5/§8.1 say so. Test api_jobs::a_dropped_requests_write_holds_a_new_claim_until_it_lands (pool store via TestServer::spawn_on_pool_with_content, a publish step's request dropped while its content write is held: the new claim is 409 owner_draining, held: true follows the write, the job is done before the claim answers its token) fails with the guard held in the handler (the claim answered 200) and passes. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all //crates/clax-content-git:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-core:all: all PASSED; //crates/clax-server:integration__1 --test_arg=api_jobs:: --runs_per_test=10: 10 of 10 passed (16 tests each).","supersedes":"be4b2d6bdd39b7760464ffbc69f837c65b51ccdc6bbb174beda31bb91bd839f8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/live_access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:52.884725Z","id":"f75d8d048bc713798c2fc714b3afce7df1358ac63ed027310cc4246a9601ea99","body":{"detail":"sees_live_pages admits any request whose connection peer is loopback (crate::auth::conn_of(ext).is_some_and(|c| is_loopback(c.peer))) and never consults crate::hosted::HostedRequest. A natively run hosted daemon is documented as sitting 'behind a proxy that terminates TLS and keeps the Host header' (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs module docs; docs/usage.md says 'Nothing is served as \"this machine\" in hosted mode'), and a Caddy, nginx or cloudflared proxy on the same host connects from 127.0.0.1. Identity::from_parts neutralises loopback trust for hosted requests (HostedRequest::identity sets local=false and drops the owner, events and viewer cookies, crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1066-1077), but sees_live_pages does not, so hide_live_pages (live_access.rs:120-133), the event and stream filters (crates/clax-server/src/routes/events.rs:120, routes/stream.rs:65 and :203) and the artifact listing (routes/artifacts.rs:259) treat every visitor, guest and member as allowed to see live pages. The extension gateway's loopback test (crates/clax-http/src/extension.rs:351-360) has the same blind spot, though it still needs a live extension credential.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":22},"content_hash":"cf0c42a31bbfbfe71e5bee54c5c995b0c3ecd92991162b0ddc2514594eccb9dc"},"suggested_fix":"Make sees_live_pages (and the extension gateway's loopback test) return false whenever the request carries a HostedRequest extension, unless it holds the daemon token, mirroring HostedRequest::identity; add a test with a hosted AppState and a loopback ConnectInfo peer asserting a live page answers 404.","summary":"sees_live_pages trusts a loopback TCP peer even on a hosted daemon, so behind a TLS proxy on the same machine every internet request may see live pages","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/socket_caps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:52.884829Z","id":"9df50fb3757c166b2a19da0151f39b7eea9f01225fa9146ae7da8b90d386b181","body":{"detail":"SocketClient::of_request keys a connection by crate::hosted::Hosted::client, which uses CF-Connecting-IP only when [hosted] behind_cloudflare is set and otherwise the TCP peer (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:434-452). docs/usage.md's [hosted] example sets behind_cloudflare = false and the module docs place the daemon behind a TLS-terminating proxy; when that proxy runs on the same host (the usual Caddy/nginx setup) every peer is 127.0.0.1, so all visitors share one Key::Address bucket of MAX_PER_ADDRESS = 128 (socket_caps.rs:34). Once 128 streams, live sockets and room sockets are open across all users, every further /api/stream or socket is refused 429 too_many_streams; one client opening 128 connections locks everyone out. The per-address abuse limits (Hosted::attempt, hosted.rs:460) collapse the same way: setup, sign-in and guest-name attempts are shared site-wide. No X-Forwarded-For or Forwarded header is honoured, and nothing warns that a loopback peer was seen in hosted mode.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":61},"end":{"line":74},"content_hash":"c0049f6b2aadd69b65fe6d34e33ffdc75332ab991f144823c554f69bba45dba3"},"suggested_fix":"Add a [hosted] option naming a trusted forwarding header (X-Forwarded-For or Forwarded, honoured only from a loopback or configured proxy peer) for Hosted::client, or refuse to start / log a warning when hosted mode sees a loopback peer without behind_cloudflare; document the requirement beside behind_cloudflare in docs/usage.md.","summary":"Without behind_cloudflare, a hosted daemon behind a same-machine proxy counts every client as the proxy's loopback address, so 128 connections site-wide exhaust the per-address cap","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/grant_auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:52.884906Z","id":"333fd585fe7ac6997d81e4c9ee8fa77b065bc814897276d71955fb5ed6e1571b","body":{"detail":"change returns Err(IndexStale) and marks the index stale only through the debug-only fail_next flag (grant_auth.rs:173-177); in a release build it always returns Ok. The module docs (grant_auth.rs:17-19) and note_stale (grant_auth.rs:311-320) describe a rebuild 'after an update that failed', and every caller threads the Result through note_stale, but no production failure can produce it. Meanwhile the one real failure mode, a panic inside f while the write lock is held, is silently absorbed: the poisoned lock is taken with unwrap_or_else(into_inner) everywhere, leaving a half-applied change without setting stale. The machinery costs reading and maintaining while protecting nothing in production.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":172},"end":{"line":182},"content_hash":"24e346c3961df9e86a8c3dfa17ac9c531bf0520f24f4ef9f0798578c20332f5b"},"suggested_fix":"Either drop the Result/IndexStale plumbing and the rebuild path, or make it real: run f under std::panic::catch_unwind(AssertUnwindSafe(..)) (or detect a poisoned lock on the next access) and set stale so the next sweep's rebuild_if_stale reloads the index from the store.","summary":"GrantIndex::change never fails in release builds, so the IndexStale / rebuild_if_stale recovery path the module docs promise runs only in tests","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:52.884967Z","id":"4cbe8ec64769ec0d6278750a1c14b26d4e9352251ce8cc8790d310a55028e564","body":{"detail":"mint_for reads `allows(st, &a, scope, ...)` in one store call (git_remotes.rs:601-608), then awaits `host.mint` (615-617), then reruns only `check_history` (618-621). check_history returns at once for an asker with no reader (git_remotes.rs:440-442: the owner, a person, a link), and for agents it checks authors, not rights. The module docs (git_remotes.rs:66-75) promise that a request narrowing rights revokes affected tokens before it answers: settle_layer (git_remotes.rs:163-179) rechecks the tokens the host lists, but a token whose mint has not returned yet is not listed, so it survives until the next recheck-triggering event or its TTL (PERSON_TTL_S 3600 s for a person, LINK_TTL_S 900 s for a link whose sharing was just withdrawn). The same race exists for a session that ends mid-mint (asker_now would say None).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":586},"end":{"line":623},"content_hash":"db18b529cd506d9f259387d43c878260353a46247dac82aa850f9fbd4c200d34"},"suggested_fix":"After the mint returns, rerun the same store-side check as before it (artifact exists, `allows`, and for agents check_history) in one store call, and revoke the minted token on any refusal, as the post-mint check_history already does; or call recheck(Some(&aid)) after minting when the visibility generation moved during the mint.","summary":"mint_for checks the asker's rights before the host mints and rechecks only the visibility history after, so a rights narrowing that lands while the mint is in flight leaves the new token live","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:52.885069Z","id":"d1b95e54dc842d71c9033f639406b58f5b6e3fe13f7fe0e0cb25ccd66a8ed9b7","body":{"detail":"The field `setup_secret` has two stacked doc lines (hosted.rs:115-116): 'The setup secret's SHA-256' and 'The setup secret, when one is set', though Hosted::new stores `sha256(secret)` (hosted.rs:307), so the second reads as if the plaintext were kept. Likewise `cookie_value` (hosted.rs:1080-1088) carries two doc paragraphs saying the same thing, while `session_token` (hosted.rs:1089), which does the work and is what the gate calls, has none. A reader auditing how the setup secret is held, or which cookie parser the gate uses, has to read the code to resolve them.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"10ecb92efc99f38489479b8513c3bb42df9e9ac402cb46287ea8a9b41f96b280"},"suggested_fix":"Keep one line on `setup_secret` ('The setup secret's SHA-256; `None` keeps setup closed'), move the single 'one cookie named `name`, `None` without one or with more than one' paragraph onto `session_token`, and make `cookie_value` a one-line alias doc (or drop the alias and call `session_token` at its users).","summary":"Hosted::setup_secret and cookie_value/session_token carry duplicated, partly contradictory doc comments","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/live_access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.259900Z","id":"73b0832ce8d3f661d41002813e69c154950ab82aee3285a40fe92e388ef091b7","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-http/src/live_access.rs:18-22 returns true for `conn_of(ext).is_some_and(|c| is_loopback(c.peer))` with no check of crate::hosted::HostedRequest, while HostedRequest::identity (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1066-1077) forces local=false for every hosted request. The hosted gate (hosted.rs gate, ~1406-1550) inserts HostedRequest but never strips the peer, and docs/usage.md:174 places the hosted daemon behind a TLS-terminating proxy, which on the same host connects from loopback. Callers that then treat the request as seeing live pages: routes/artifacts.rs:259 (listing filter `!local && a.kind == KIND_LIVE`), routes/events.rs:120, routes/stream.rs:65 and :203, routes/working.rs:211, and the hide_live_pages middleware (live_access.rs:120-133). The extension gateway's loopback test (crates/clax-http/src/extension.rs:351) likewise uses peer_of alone. Kind concern fits: exposure needs a same-host proxy and a live page on the hosted daemon.","kind":"comment","references":"f75d8d048bc713798c2fc714b3afce7df1358ac63ed027310cc4246a9601ea99","summary":"confirmed: sees_live_pages admits any loopback peer and ignores HostedRequest","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/socket_caps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.260089Z","id":"19e92e13db4463465e9118481a1c1477fd7f37977797d7629ec3e6e920bf917d","body":{"detail":"SocketClient::of_request (crates/clax-http/src/socket_caps.rs:61-74) keys by crate::hosted::client_key(h.client(..)); Hosted::client (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:434-452) reads CF-Connecting-IP only when behind_cloudflare (or wasm32), else peer_of, so a same-host proxy makes every peer loopback. MAX_PER_ADDRESS = 128 (socket_caps.rs:34). Hosted::attempt (hosted.rs:460-468) uses the same client key for the rate limits. `grep -n -i forwarded crates/clax-http/src/*.rs` finds no X-Forwarded-For/Forwarded handling. docs/usage.md:174-180 asks for a TLS-terminating proxy and shows behind_cloudflare = false, with no warning about a loopback proxy.","kind":"comment","references":"9df50fb3757c166b2a19da0151f39b7eea9f01225fa9146ae7da8b90d386b181","summary":"confirmed: behind a same-host proxy without behind_cloudflare every client shares one 128-connection address bucket","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/grant_auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.260255Z","id":"7cd3403dd6548236648cd6d23669c6b0a2ef3172e9bcb6d392b763c10bb1a33c","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-http/src/grant_auth.rs:172-182: the only Err(IndexStale) path is under #[cfg(debug_assertions)] (fail_next, set by fail_next_change at :166-170); otherwise it takes the write lock with unwrap_or_else(|e| e.into_inner()), runs f and returns Ok. The module docs (:17-19) and note_stale (:311-320) describe a rebuild after a failed update, which a release build never produces; a panic in f under the lock is absorbed by the into_inner calls (:113, :140, :150, :178, :248, :270, :289) without setting stale. Suggestion kind fits.","kind":"comment","references":"333fd585fe7ac6997d81e4c9ee8fa77b065bc814897276d71955fb5ed6e1571b","summary":"confirmed: GrantIndex::change can only fail through the debug-only fail_next flag","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.260413Z","id":"3f0706e6a34fc64dc27e249c714b7eb0a8c348670c293259b582246845a2a756","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs:601-608 reads get_artifact and `allows` in one store call; :615-617 awaits host.mint; :618-621 reruns only check_history, which returns Ok at once when asker.reader() is None (:440-442). settle_layer (:163-179) and recheck (:729-759) revoke only tokens that host.held() lists, and rights_changed revokes by holder through host.revoke_held, so a token the host registers after that recheck or revocation ran survives until its TTL (PERSON_TTL_S 3600 at :110, LINK_TTL_S 900 at :116). The module docs (:66-75) promise revocation before the narrowing request answers. Narrow race; concern fits.","kind":"comment","references":"4cbe8ec64769ec0d6278750a1c14b26d4e9352251ce8cc8790d310a55028e564","summary":"confirmed: mint_for checks rights only before host.mint and rechecks only history after","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.260567Z","id":"b3eb5a11349ad1b3a9ecd59cfe505f8ab132d9c25aa2e8ac1590994730394487","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:115-116 stacks 'The setup secret's SHA-256; `None` keeps setup closed.' and 'The setup secret, when one is set (`None`: setup stays closed).' on `setup_secret`, while Hosted::new stores `setup_secret.filter(..).map(sha256)` (:307). cookie_value (:1080-1088) carries two doc paragraphs saying the same, and `pub fn session_token` (:1089) has no doc comment. Suggestion kind fits.","kind":"comment","references":"d1b95e54dc842d71c9033f639406b58f5b6e3fe13f7fe0e0cb25ccd66a8ed9b7","summary":"confirmed: setup_secret and cookie_value carry stacked, overlapping doc comments; session_token has none","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:25:45.662858Z","id":"3adcaebf04ac0f161ef55acd4e9ab37e220c115bf87334256bea9bf50ce872f8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f6ded05fe","summary":"Fixed: mint_for rechecks the holder (artifact live, asker_now, allows) after the host mints and revokes the token on refusal; person_allows refuses a revoked person. api_git_tokens::a_narrowing_that_lands_while_a_token_is_minted_refuses_and_revokes_it passes (200 before, 403 now).","supersedes":"4cbe8ec64769ec0d6278750a1c14b26d4e9352251ce8cc8790d310a55028e564","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/grant_auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:25:45.713311Z","id":"0edc22f1b145dbac07173d53c71f567d117fdef876b1b668d7865907f805976f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:04e1560b2","summary":"Fixed: GrantIndex::change runs under catch_unwind and marks the index stale on a panic or a poisoned lock; grant_auth::tests::a_change_that_panics_marks_the_index_for_a_rebuild_and_the_next_one_applies and a_panic_under_the_lock_elsewhere_… pass (failed before).","supersedes":"333fd585fe7ac6997d81e4c9ee8fa77b065bc814897276d71955fb5ed6e1571b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/socket_caps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:17:18.738261Z","id":"d07faaab192ca82e699e7ab71556056e9a3100c49253e2d958ae579744359325","body":{"detail":"Done: Hosted::note_peer (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs, called from gate after the Host check) logs one warning when a request for the public or content host comes from a loopback peer with behind_cloudflare off (requests naming a local host, the CLI's and agents', are not counted), and docs/usage.md's hosted-mode paragraph says every client then shares one address's limits and its 128 streams and sockets. Hosted::client still keys by the TCP peer, so the shared bucket remains.\n\nOptions:\n(a) A [hosted] option naming a trusted forwarding header (X-Forwarded-For or Forwarded), honoured only when the TCP peer is loopback (or a configured proxy address), taking the address the proxy appended; Hosted::client uses it for Hosted::attempt and SocketClient::of_request. Fixes Caddy/nginx/cloudflared on the same host. Risk: a proxy that does not overwrite the header lets a client pick its own address and dodge the limits.\n(b) Refuse to serve (or to start) in hosted mode when a loopback peer names the public host and neither behind_cloudflare nor a forwarding header is configured. Safest, but breaks same-host deployments that work today.\n(c) Keep the warning alone.\n\nRecommendation: (a), with no default header (the operator names it), honoured from a loopback peer only, and the warning kept for when it is unset.","kind":"comment","references":"9df50fb3757c166b2a19da0151f39b7eea9f01225fa9146ae7da8b90d386b181","summary":"Partly addressed: a same-host proxy is now logged and documented; how clients behind it are told apart needs the owner's call","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:36:49.749765Z","id":"d6d3192c30b295b56f415623c3ef6341f8b32945e4def8eadc48136a4c6637fe","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:05b23a6fa","summary":"Fixed: setup_secret, cookie_value and session_token each carry one doc comment (doc-only).","supersedes":"d1b95e54dc842d71c9033f639406b58f5b6e3fe13f7fe0e0cb25ccd66a8ed9b7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/live_access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:36:49.957653Z","id":"520f04759aa932f041b05a9f948407dd27e1164657af38176fd7837f89e2838f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2f798c2ab","summary":"Fixed: auth::loopback_peer counts a loopback peer only on a non-hosted request; live_access and auth unit tests and api_hosted::a_live_page_is_hidden_from_visitors_though_they_connect_from_loopback pass.","supersedes":"f75d8d048bc713798c2fc714b3afce7df1358ac63ed027310cc4246a9601ea99","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:10:58.535714Z","id":"a24163203238c92e139f51f53530274230534c03a23c714b2222331893198641","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:503-503, record fced511a.\n\napi_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":566},"end":{"line":566},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","supersedes":"0fc5b5a306904dd9f8d626833098b4c83ea8833e4bd8268df25b8d34ae714499","tags":["people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:10:58.757856Z","id":"18483473fec681267aa5ae14df64f95a65be784dad0b4ba868d1d8e68721d409","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:998-998, record 3c0ad45d.\n\nEvery handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":1166},"end":{"line":1166},"content_hash":"0084401cde97b2431fc0a50fda577f15da02d5950c956b6bd243c5b7d069ce7d"},"summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"9b2312dfb677c9c5e21ef1ed722dbbb403f86b50dc1b6a39d0c1ccbb0cf57518","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:06:31.747271Z","id":"a415d05e47354eb66bab985ed257dd744ed151738c15d4447ce2df82186fa913","body":{"detail":"The site routes of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md ('What a site host serves') replace this: the current version at the site's root, Clax's paths under /_clax/, and nothing rewritten to /c/<id>/. Until then a site host reaches only content, /_clax/*, /_blob/* and /healthz, which is also why the Origin checks that still use the localhost-only artifact_host (crates/clax-http/src/viewer.rs:99, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs:150) cannot be reached from a site host under a configured [hosted] site_domain. Once /_clax/api/ is served on site hosts, those checks must ask AppState::sites instead, and artifact_host goes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"660a3134809d67d4c886c2528380c38aaefecc5aff2509a393689bf7fb475821"},"summary":"site_layer still rewrites /v/* and /draft/* to /c/<id>/… and answers every other site path 404","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:17:42.964566Z","id":"0b03eb3d40520028249f1cb80e8eaab37f3e99e9a8b35f5c13fbb46319764271","body":{"detail":"The site routes of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md ('What a site host serves') replace this: the current version at the site's root, Clax's paths under /_clax/, and nothing rewritten to /c/<id>/. Until then a site host reaches only content, /_clax/*, /_blob/* and /healthz, which is also why the Origin checks that still use the localhost-only artifact_host (crates/clax-http/src/viewer.rs:99, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs:150) cannot be reached from a site host under a configured [hosted] site_domain. Once /_clax/api/ is served on site hosts, those checks must ask AppState::sites instead, and artifact_host goes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":165},"content_hash":"660a3134809d67d4c886c2528380c38aaefecc5aff2509a393689bf7fb475821"},"summary":"site_layer still rewrites /v/* and /draft/* to /c/<id>/… and answers every other site path 404","supersedes":"a415d05e47354eb66bab985ed257dd744ed151738c15d4447ce2df82186fa913","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:18:19.108820Z","id":"47529f02bf2d0554b0d5ecdcb53f8a57d9167d7ea47adcd2137a2dd5ff0cee6c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0b03eb3d40520028249f1cb80e8eaab37f3e99e9a8b35f5c13fbb46319764271","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":165},"content_hash":"660a3134809d67d4c886c2528380c38aaefecc5aff2509a393689bf7fb475821"},"summary":"The Worker is in scope too: crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs:158 decides whether a request is on the public host with clax_http::host::artifact_host, which knows <id>.localhost alone, so a site host under a configured site domain is not recognized there either. It moves to the configured lookup with the others.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:18:19.109045Z","id":"f6f9d0cf78d8a14e1f1f14efbb84ae5289614bf0a18322870fd828a44c843369","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0b03eb3d40520028249f1cb80e8eaab37f3e99e9a8b35f5c13fbb46319764271","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":165},"content_hash":"660a3134809d67d4c886c2528380c38aaefecc5aff2509a393689bf7fb475821"},"summary":"Where this resolves, in docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md: Task 2 ('Site routes: the current version at the root, Clax's under /_clax/') removes the rewriting in site_layer; Task 7 ('/_clax/api/ on the site host, scoped by the host') moves the Origin checks of crates/clax-http/src/viewer.rs:99 and crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs:150 to AppState::sites, and Task 11 (the Worker's site hosts) does the same for crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs:158; artifact_host goes with its last caller.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:26:43.829269Z","id":"c2b6acc622c457751eaa780bf99c72228c248f456f384ad866de386caf18a127","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0b03eb3d40520028249f1cb80e8eaab37f3e99e9a8b35f5c13fbb46319764271","summary":"The rewriting part is fixed in f4c42b80: site_layer only inserts SiteRequest (and Referrer-Policy: no-referrer on the response) and leaves the path as it is; crates/clax-server/src/router.rs by_host sends a site request to crates/clax-server/src/routes/site.rs alone. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__2 --test_arg=api_site:: passes all of api_site (the_root_serves_the_current_version, an_unknown_clax_path_is_404, the_public_host_serves_no_content, ...). Still open on this thread: artifact_host's callers named in replies 47529f02 and f6f9d0cf (crates/clax-http/src/viewer.rs:99, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs:150, crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs:158), which Tasks 7 and 11 of docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md move to AppState::sites; close the thread once they have.","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:07:28.797362Z","id":"d80c7e2e195798453cc3a2a3f8e6725479607db9b66002c03e5626d6a366c2c4","body":{"detail":"MovingAppData checks that the artifact is live (Store::app_data_state) before the call, but delete_artifact_async removes the directory after its transaction commits; a call that passed the check and reaches AppData::open (crates/clax-store/src/app_data/mod.rs, create_dir_all) after the removal leaves a stray store for a deleted artifact. Opening per call also costs a connection and WAL setup each time; a cache of open stores would need the delete to close them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":45},"end":{"line":58},"content_hash":"fe4d852122fabc8fc689fd883f327bb713ff85c452ebedf4e3cb2a9bf9c77939"},"summary":"LocalAppData opens the artifact's data.sqlite on every call, and a call racing the artifact's delete can recreate artifacts/<id>/data.sqlite after the directory was removed","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:07:28.797412Z","id":"7f522106216ce55529ea17a35a1144fffb2fe8e6b2197e0cfb8371e4f8f90e25","body":{"detail":"AppState::assemble (crates/clax-http/src/state.rs) sets app_data from default_host; the Worker's own host over an artifact Durable Object (AppData::open_on) is not built yet. MovingAppData wraps NoAppData there so the move and folds are already in place when the Worker's host replaces it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":186},"end":{"line":202},"content_hash":"00b89d305a6fab21679aa77b783e36b3be6195a0c4060399290981cb83bbf245"},"summary":"On wasm32 the default host is NoAppData, so every db route fails on the Worker until crates/clax-worker sets AppState::app_data to its own Durable Object host","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:31:59.280627Z","id":"cd3aafe6e8368a26810a9b559052689bd9d7c6fe5024ec9d39132bbf9556f896","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dfde3cd1","summary":"Fixed: only Import makes a store file (AppData::open_existing answers NotFound otherwise), and a move whose artifact was deleted meanwhile erases the store its import made. //crates/clax-http:clax_http_lib_test passes app_data_host::tests::only_an_import_makes_a_store and a_delete_during_the_move_leaves_no_store. The per-call open cost is recorded on its own.","supersedes":"d80c7e2e195798453cc3a2a3f8e6725479607db9b66002c03e5626d6a366c2c4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:31:59.585156Z","id":"3ff6feb5e7c7314acea52354884daccb41a91a4b9696a8d97070e04464917651","body":{"detail":"AppState::assemble sets app_data from default_host, which on wasm32 wraps NoAppData. crates/clax-worker must set AppState::app_data to a host over a Durable Object per artifact (AppData::open_on) before a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":330},"end":{"line":343},"content_hash":"0361a8346a283af3b6e887a7dfd7aab15af4a88f55fc3a82fa67c57906b3b449"},"summary":"This branch must not deploy to the Worker before the Worker's own artifact-store host lands: there the default is NoAppData and every db route fails","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:31:59.585243Z","id":"38ee5f21ab1b56c2088b6d9661fddb207ec1f0d2181086a7b81913f89c7ff050","body":{"detail":"A cache of open stores would save it, but the artifact's delete (FsContent::delete_artifact removing artifacts/<id>/) would then have to close the cached connection first.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"6e87d0e849cc5dde6a37901309663f916c831376f175d5b61e1b3f2fbb58b79b"},"summary":"LocalAppData opens the artifact's data.sqlite on every call: a connection and its WAL setup per db operation","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:31:59.585303Z","id":"60abbf154dcc5a4097759b061a99feff19928fe4f3b01caad7ebf94a6ef26799","body":{"detail":"MovingAppData::copies_once runs once per artifact per process; the state read (Store::app_data_state) is a separate store hop from the route's own (Decided in crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs), since the host behind AppDataHost::call takes only the artifact and the operation. Passing the state in would need the trait to take it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":261},"end":{"line":274},"content_hash":"1705fce1d2402451810da4c4e925df5d2d4417d0a6de0fe1f39ba8b682a55bbf"},"summary":"Every artifact's first call after a start makes an extra AuditSince call to make up lost audit copies, and every db call still makes its own instance read of the artifact's move state","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:38:44.071640Z","id":"69fc7645894ae17f6f29d6df89eb43589f700b469a499859dfa27bc03bdc443a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"60abbf154dcc5a4097759b061a99feff19928fe4f3b01caad7ebf94a6ef26799","summary":"A copy made up late (at the next change, or at the artifact's first call after a start) lands after the tool.call it was made under recorded its produced list, so that list leaves the late record out though the record carries the call's call_id.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:38:44.071819Z","id":"550305d7f725cd40cabdbe7427e9f87e309efc107444691fcf07e0ee1be6e319","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"cd3aafe6e8368a26810a9b559052689bd9d7c6fe5024ec9d39132bbf9556f896","summary":"Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-http:clax_http_lib_test passes app_data_host::tests::only_an_import_makes_a_store and app_data_host::tests::a_delete_during_the_move_leaves_no_store (80 passed at 477bf54d, which also checks the emptied artifacts/<id>/ directory goes).","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:36:21.299988Z","id":"11ae2ec26b4d88db80ea9ac9ccc8b6f6e630459794cf74a9841e389d3de1fbd1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:737442a3","summary":"Fixed in 737442a3: content keys are gone (content_key, asset_key, clip_key and stamp_content_keys removed from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs). Content is served on its artifact's site host alone, where the site session holder's right is checked on every request, so losing a right, a share or the link refuses the next request; the old keyed addresses (/c/.../k/..., /_clip/...) are 404 and an asset's old address only redirects (301) to its site; a clip is read with the reader's own credential. Evidence: bazelisk test of //crates/clax-server:integration__1 to __6 passes revoking_a_share_ends_the_site_session_on_the_next_request and a_link_viewer_reads_without_signing_in_until_the_link_is_turned_off (api_site_access), content_is_served_on_its_site_alone_and_keyed_addresses_are_gone, an_old_keyed_asset_url_only_redirects_to_its_site and a_clip_is_served_to_its_reader_alone (api_hosted).","supersedes":"ad4d8d8c97b30ea324cdbd7218826481a8ddbad720b28cae710d7325b0f14f3a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:15:08.315308Z","id":"2b656624329adf3df2f3db247f2b43e03f2a1e39a990fabcdd1ca62ec7e39e91","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ae27855a","summary":"The Worker sets AppState::app_data to MovingAppData over crate::app_data::WorkerAppData (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs Instance::build), one AppDataDo per artifact (AppData::open_on on DoPageStore). Evidence: node crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs passes 'the document lives in the artifact's object and not in the instance's database' and 'the API reads the document back from the artifact's object' (a PUT /api/artifacts/<id>/docs/tasks/t1 under wrangler dev --local).","supersedes":"7f522106216ce55529ea17a35a1144fffb2fe8e6b2197e0cfb8371e4f8f90e25","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:15:08.335605Z","id":"a2d6a528474fbbd8d045ed4368b303b18f87599c832dd8d101b0388dcc105f46","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ae27855a","summary":"The Worker no longer runs NoAppData: crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs replaces the default host with MovingAppData over WorkerAppData (crates/clax-worker/src/app_data.rs), and deleting an artifact erases its object. Evidence: node crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs passes the db steps and 'deleting an artifact erases its object's store'; deploy.mjs's guard (workerReadsSiteDomain) now finds the Worker's read of SITE_DOMAIN.","supersedes":"3ff6feb5e7c7314acea52354884daccb41a91a4b9696a8d97070e04464917651","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.210326Z","id":"b0159d89c908a1f2da6e9aa8a64a0e5e0db5d4e236e2be189c66329c9cba0b40","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:565-591, record 4585fb7a.\n\nThe keyed address is an HMAC of <aid>/<tid> (clip_key), not a hash of the PNG: a thread's clip is written once and never changes for that (artifact, thread) pair (a move to another artifact makes a new pair, crates/clax-core/src/store/site.rs put_clip), so the address is immutable without reading every clip to hash it for a listing. Clips stay stored once per thread (ContentStore::put_clip). The hosted shell still loads clip_url (GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/threads/<tid>/clip, credentialed, Cache-Control private, max-age=3600); thread views carry clip_link only for agents (VisFor::of in crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs). Pointing the shell's <img> at the keyed address would make one cacheable URL for both, and needs browser verification of the hosted shell.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":610},"end":{"line":636},"content_hash":"4ef566a7f6b579607ca61e72bcc3b70574f6290b0dce5ccc923eb7513bfe633e"},"summary":"Key a clip's address by its content hash, and have the hosted shell load clips from it","supersedes":"924f246c3d11dfd9cdf02556bed14c4a9b5b18118a7d4c6c868b5a919429fec2","tags":["hosted","revisit:hosted shell clip loads show in the time-to-usable budget, or a clip's bytes may change for its thread","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.228915Z","id":"b5d7883007c32a878ede23828dd21f90dc1fa836389bf44ef8d635e5815f86be","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:669-674, record 6b80c3e5.\n\nThe gate could require /c/<aid>/draft/k/<content key of the base version>/<agent>/<token>/…, so a draft URL is also bound to a key the daemon derives. Not taken: the draft token is already 128 random bits minted per revision (clax_core::drafts::new_token), handed only to people who may read the artifact, and it expires with the revision, which a content key never does; a second key adds a path segment the shell's draftSrc (web/shell/src/view/draft-model.ts) and the artifact host rewrite (crates/clax-server/src/host.rs) would carry for no capability the token lacks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":714},"end":{"line":719},"content_hash":"3eb6e5e71cb8f25d42801db35df391e5cb63b49c9661a3034fa54c8a8c5d32db"},"summary":"Draft URLs keyed by the version's content key as well as the draft token","supersedes":"2b006cc0e57d1bd9a98cc8d7e7d29b29e8ed2b344bd59cf97af640eb110821f3","tags":["hosted","drafts","revisit:a draft token is logged, persisted or handed to anyone who may not read the artifact","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.250729Z","id":"d5b795e80d4fe154ed315f532eeb44f05cace02a615154e4fdcea1063370cf40","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:933-937, record a625cb63.\n\nmember_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":978},"end":{"line":982},"content_hash":"11a6d516f89aca58a56ce0b74606965d429431759b9528b5f9e41f848acf059f"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","supersedes":"63ce5763c0196d3bba5e418b059982564b9fe0d3069fcdf8a0d21bdcd088927e","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.271720Z","id":"3da6e5e82737f85a811601d17ccb528093c04103f2b1dc267facd7c522ab273f","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1181-1183, record 5d1ab740.\n\nThe prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1226},"end":{"line":1228},"content_hash":"eb2ee61fc1f30c9d5fbc64de9d7d23e62b6ed111716b76f7bac3b80e5bd50a7f"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","supersedes":"4f449f18717d16fa8462adf699146a5355235181cab5bd661d6d2cd09923b033","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.289657Z","id":"de33a2ab0f229556d49d8e0a826b18c85037f7c1bb30e5cc96ef5d25960b78b2","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1607-1615, record 5be58509.\n\nPUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1654},"end":{"line":1662},"content_hash":"7a476461c501f781b8050a6c407b4957edf0b5b0b0e10511b4b8a0fcf190fdec"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","supersedes":"ddaee3f9dbacd808b879f2923a80d54cbfe33c1412ad1171fdad9b4e6608e4e6","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.588846Z","id":"c2022c63f2969f16db7ca867692e2875bc8c87063d9408a7b7d49f76dac23cd5","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:197-200, record ed323928.\n\nLimits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":213},"content_hash":"e773e1438242b272aff7abb4426e25b6868af8c1d503cc1f0ab28083fc52603f"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","supersedes":"930a2cdfdfee1ac179d6d28c701931c7cda59a419ca69a2e84bfa48c27d7b68f","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:39:37.372949Z","id":"470b362e94d3e4b05f824087a1040e2a0a0b4c08223010ddf803e053a5f7c345","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0a1a0d4b04504252c8f9703038c055b7e0ee47f052ebc29bf8a1458c77a32cd3","summary":"Proposed close for the owner: since 86ec4f43 a local daemon refuses every request of another machine that is not a connected person's (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs local_peers; crates/clax-server/tests/api_content.rs a_lan_viewer_is_refused), so LAN viewers who are not connected write nothing. What is left is the reply's scope: a connected person's browser on another machine, and a hosted daemon's guests, still write with no rate limit.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/socket_caps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:39:37.373128Z","id":"ad48e4dc81e4661b0748c0760d33244dde6375948970d10d2f906982889735ca","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"49249c3c5d999900f56c0b5dfe5246c98731877939e2790aa8e952278e750a12","summary":"Proposed close for the owner: since 86ec4f43 a local daemon refuses the streams and sockets of another machine's viewer who is not connected (403 forbidden_host, crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs local_peers; crates/clax-server/tests/api_content.rs a_lan_viewer_is_refused). A connected person's browser on another machine still opens any number; keep it open if that matters.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:39:37.373282Z","id":"d7221ed8b65ef372d4a0dc82fc493b2c5030f90683a1f9a62e03682917d9b9f5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"18483473fec681267aa5ae14df64f95a65be784dad0b4ba868d1d8e68721d409","summary":"Proposed close for the owner: since 86ec4f43 a LAN viewer's cookie request no longer reaches an agent route (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs local_peers answers 403 forbidden_host first; crates/clax-server/tests/api_content.rs a_lan_viewer_is_refused). A connected person's cookie from another machine now costs one viewer read in local_peers before Agent<N> reads it again.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:39:37.373858Z","id":"5aa5c8a7894e8bb753fffdf37984e28d7015653ad0984725f4117a8cb7f0b5f0","body":{"detail":"local_peers admits a non-loopback peer that carries a grant credential or Clax-Signature, calls /api/grants…, opens /connect/b/<code>, or holds a clax_viewer cookie of an unrevoked person. Such a browser reaches the gallery, inbox, People and comments, but no artifact's page: the sites are <id>.localhost, which resolve on the person's own machine, and the shell shows 'This page opens only on the machine that runs Clax' (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts elsewhere). The owner's bearer token from another machine is refused (crates/clax-server/tests/api_live.rs live_pages_and_all_else_are_refused_to_lan_callers). docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md says a local daemon 'serves this machine alone': refusing persons' browsers too would also end their approvals and raises, which only a browser can make (docs/usage.md People). Decision needed: keep persons' browsers from the LAN, or serve this machine alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"fa857c397abca7e0d1d8faddb6e536a1a061a53ea30d1b56e9a280d2f177c1c0"},"summary":"A local daemon still serves a connected person's browser on another machine, which gets the shell but no page","tags":["status:needs-decision","site-origins","lan","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T16:28:15.055780Z","id":"a1121ad2c8bd281c2f523337a858ab521c293017cf5ebecee71e0b076551cb33","body":{"detail":"SiteCredentials::check runs when Event::Access or Event::SiteAccess reaches the socket (crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs RoomCheck::ask), before the next message after one (the daemon), and when the Worker reopens it. A site session that ends by time (SITE_SESSION_TTL_SECS unused; each check renews it) or a browser session that expires on its own TTL emits no event, so a socket opened on it stays open until the next such event or wake, where it closes 4403 revoked; a request on the site is refused at once either way. Accepted: no right was removed, only a session aged.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":158},"content_hash":"05c3343d2aeb248ea315510ad694530716d980722d78cc54c7b6fbf4f8040d90"},"summary":"A site room socket is checked again on access changes and wakes, not when its site or browser session merely expires","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T18:24:59.660737Z","id":"a2bc156c306600423c10a0c7be049efd63e77186662d7dc5e781e5a50fcc1be2","body":{"detail":"SiteCredentials::check runs when Event::Access, Event::SiteAccess or a new version reaches a holder's socket (crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs RoomCheck::ask), before the next message after one, and when the Worker reopens it; each check renews the site session. A socket's own messages renew it too, at most every SITE_SESSION_RENEW_SECS (crates/clax-store/src/site_sessions.rs; RoomCheck::renewal_due and RoomCheck::renew, on the daemon and the Worker), so a socket in use outlives SITE_SESSION_TTL_SECS (test: api_site_access::a_site_room_socket_in_use_outlives_its_sessions_first_hour). A socket that sends nothing for SITE_SESSION_TTL_SECS lets its session expire, and the next such event or wake closes it 4403 revoked, as that test's owner socket shows; its page has to reopen through a new site session. A browser session that expires on its own TTL emits no event either, and closes it the same way. Accepted: the room client (web/bridge/src/caps/room-socket.ts) sends no keep-alive, and a page that sent nothing for an hour loses only its socket, not a right.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"05c3343d2aeb248ea315510ad694530716d980722d78cc54c7b6fbf4f8040d90"},"summary":"A site room socket left unused past its site session's TTL closes at the next access change or wake, though its holder still reads","supersedes":"a1121ad2c8bd281c2f523337a858ab521c293017cf5ebecee71e0b076551cb33","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:39:58.705743Z","id":"479fe3d689c2163c0ffdc8b6cafd703cbbc2b9d39c3d47af7b8ab0d3c46984bf","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"930a2cdfdfee1ac179d6d28c701931c7cda59a419ca69a2e84bfa48c27d7b68f","summary":"Counting app installs (Attempt::Install, 10 at once, one back a minute per client) is held in the same in-memory Limits: a restart or a Worker wake gives every client its attempts back. What survives is bounded by app_installs counting each (artifact, install ID) once (crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs record_install).","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:22:50.565598Z","id":"f2415df240c8904293bf1bbb53ee8d6de293bbe39bdcb552c6fd38d3d9eaba25","body":{"detail":"verify_bearer hands a person-device grant a PersonDevice whose who is the person's member session (Store::person_device_viewer), and crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs browser_or_device takes it as that session: may_share and session_reads read the person's rights, never the grant's narrowing. Narrowing applies to a grant's sessions (Store::grant_caller); the Clax app's token opens none on these routes. A person who narrows the app's token on People still lets it share every artifact they made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2039},"end":{"line":2060},"content_hash":"ac6260549d2bff9f04aa3a9c74651b357e21dee778ee91f1b320200da366acc8"},"suggested_fix":"Intersect with Store::grant_caller(gid, None)'s rights in person_device_viewer's caller, or hide Narrow for kind device on People.","summary":"A person's device acts on sharing with its person's full rights: narrowing its grant (PUT /api/people/me/grants/<gid>/narrow) does not limit it","tags":["security","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:10:27.064947Z","id":"bd630904894f2045da06948f8763182657307b0a0eaa5642bbafc63c38126418","body":{"detail":"Replacing this arm's MemberRights::of_session with None leaves every test in //crates/clax-server:integration__4, __5 and __6 passing; only a probe outside the suite failed (Sam's device, GET /api/artifacts/<id>/head of an app Ada never shared, answered 200 with its title and content_sha256 instead of 403 not_permitted). With the arm as committed the probe answers 403 not_permitted on head, versions/1, versions/1/bundle and versions/1/files/index.html. api_remotes_app::a_device_reads_shared_apps_as_its_person covers a shared app, a plain agent token and a revoked device, not an unshared one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1236},"end":{"line":1240},"content_hash":"168ebaffccd2a2759e8628d2bd1ea01faa84e93af5bed317cf7063ec4fceb023"},"suggested_fix":"Add to a_device_reads_shared_apps_as_its_person: an app of Ada's not shared with Sam, read with Sam's device token on the four PERSON_DEVICE_ROUTES read routes, each 403.","summary":"No test pins that a person's device reads only what its person may: with the device's MemberRights removed the branch's suite still passes","tags":["review","security","app-push","severity:minor","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:10:27.065461Z","id":"be4126cc4cef2f9e862940d5f1d0ae9f40acd3c7ab5e7e5b656fe57e5c37716e","body":{"detail":"PERSON_DEVICE_ROUTES (agent.rs) now holds GET head, versions/{n}, versions/{n}/bundle and versions/{n}/files/{*path}; on them Identity::caller (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs, the device branch) answers Caller::Person and the Agent extractor limits it by MemberRights::of_session, the person's rights, so a narrowing on the device's grant (PUT /api/people/me/grants/<gid>/narrow) limits neither its sharing nor these reads.","kind":"comment","references":"f2415df240c8904293bf1bbb53ee8d6de293bbe39bdcb552c6fd38d3d9eaba25","summary":"The device's reads now take the same path: a narrowed device token reads every artifact its person may","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:12:20.940077Z","id":"58b282099b2bf59623a0b3e142b937526867a08428c1e978b700425f429ebd10","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:eca9bf59b","summary":"api_remotes_app::a_device_reads_shared_apps_as_its_person now checks Sam's device gets 403 not_permitted on head, versions/1, versions/1/bundle and versions/1/files/index.html of an app of Ada's not shared with him; it passes under bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__6 and fails at api_remotes_app.rs:1341 (200 on head) with the device's MemberRights::of_session replaced by None in crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs.","supersedes":"bd630904894f2045da06948f8763182657307b0a0eaa5642bbafc63c38126418","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/limits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.101950Z","id":"79971760dddfbbfe6448e44898093f5dc540a17ef8839760f660cd5d635d7651","body":{"detail":"On the hosted side a bearer-token PUT of a bundle is read by crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs read_unverified within read_deadline(n) = GRACE (10 s) + 1 s per MiB: 42 s for 32 MiB, about 6.4 Mbit/s sustained; past it the gate answers 408 timeout (agent.rs timeout()). The core's forward (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs put_bundle via crates/clax-server/src/public.rs forward_with, REQUEST_TIMEOUT 120 s) passes the 408 through. apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart _transient counts only status 0 and 5xx as worth retrying, so the app drops the pending bundle and shows the refusal: the public version was already published by the push, and recipients are offered no update for it (only versions carrying a bundle are offered). A phone uploading at 2 Mbit/s needs about 135 s for 32 MiB, so the effective bundle cap depends on bandwidth, not MAX_BUNDLE_BYTES. Separate from the Worker's 16 MiB body cap (record 9518a701 on crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"1a6d7de2245c94eccba320a1e58adb683b53da8f26616315580a571ffde1fa02"},"suggested_fix":"Give the bundle route a read deadline sized for slow uplinks (MIN_RATE alone, or a per-route deadline), keep the core's timeout above it, and have the app treat 408 as transient.","summary":"A bundle near the 32 MiB cap cannot be uploaded on a slow uplink: the hosted agent gate refuses it 408 timeout, and the app then drops the bundle, leaving the published version without one","tags":["review","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:08:31.106697Z","id":"ff4ed7d34fe4ed38f2c5c3712f085c45be9c1e5fa6e8c0cf8d7809763c4c3719","body":{"detail":"Making the narrowing bind a device on crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs browser_or_device routes means intersecting the grant's narrowing with the person's MemberRights in may_share and session_reads, with identity carried from clax-http verify_bearer (PersonDevice). Two choices are the owner's: (1) the hosted Clax owner's own device has no MemberRights row to intersect with, so what does a narrowed owner device allow? (2) Refusing narrow on device grants instead (PUT /api/people/me/grants/<gid>/narrow answers an error for a person-device grant) would also drop the narrowing that does bind the device's agent-route publishes (Store::grant_caller). Left unchanged.","kind":"comment","references":"f2415df240c8904293bf1bbb53ee8d6de293bbe39bdcb552c6fd38d3d9eaba25","summary":"Needs a decision: how a narrowed device grant meets its person's rights on sharing","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:14:21.447938Z","id":"83e83a67f127a741717e00b65c55ad490e0bd45d6ee969351b207d922001e9fd","body":{"detail":"ViewLimiter keeps the last recorded time per viewer, kind and subject for five minutes (docs/contract.md 'Toolpath journal and export'); it is pruned past 4096 entries. Views are never lost, only recorded more often than once a window across restarts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":414},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"844f09ab8b6e89f13e3e507b311eb219276a0ae929a785cdd78005ad9896c9ab"},"summary":"The view limiter is memory only, per process (per Durable Object incarnation on the Worker): a restart or an eviction records the next view again","tags":["claxbot","audit","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:25:51.754015Z","id":"f1f2b2a55e1743bbc46e5fd9f432620d7fa5865589887e3704b12dd63f865d88","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"83e83a67f127a741717e00b65c55ad490e0bd45d6ee969351b207d922001e9fd","summary":"Since 33be80f5 the limiter is bounded (4,096 SHA-256 keys, expired entries pruned first, then the oldest evicted; test the_limiter_stays_bounded_evicting_the_oldest) and keys a LAN viewer by its viewer ID, so an eviction under load also records a view again early. The memory-only, per-process property this record names is unchanged.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.715365Z","id":"4af60633c0e68b7e88e490427b950bd7b32cf5497852ab10d650b2e0734db5aa","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs:153-171, record 36bf936e.\n\nis_grant_request includes Bearer cxa_…, and verify_layer admits it wherever a route's need! admits grants, so a script holding an agent token can call the API directly with the same rights its MCP tools have. The prototype (hosted/src/mcp/server.ts) took the token only at /mcp. The rights are identical either way; restricting it to in-process requests from the adapter would need a marker the loopback sets.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":154},"end":{"line":172},"content_hash":"e6eb9b5cd97f310ac94ca698005b960357df7ef98121b5cc7bb8c8f5000f777c"},"summary":"An agent token is an agent credential on every route a grant may reach, not only through the MCP adapter","supersedes":"a5c04cf14514c3880ce8df7d155e983784e5af984cc3cd3b0f047f73bf85a0b2","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.771135Z","id":"56e65d4c1bf9d7a3d8530314cb560a2cfc79d7156a92c34a8fd5fb59b422d048","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs:403-424, record 7aa11f30.\n\ncrate::seats::subscribe (called by POST /api/stream/<id>, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update) takes the artifact's seat for connection stream:<id> when the stream holds none of its live topics yet. If two calls add live topics of the same artifact at once and one then fails (TooMany, Hidden), its rollback leaves the seat the other call's topics rely on. The shell's hub sends one change at a time per stream, so this needs a hand-made client.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":165},"end":{"line":186},"content_hash":"4c1d002bb08b1e78d10906ff498e81fd66cd9f8f4590b4773cb4c6d540bb79bd"},"summary":"Two concurrent subscription changes of one stream can leave it on an artifact's live topics without its seat","supersedes":"66ee3d55f637a69b899684765c1c986fa2a79fec7987528ee094b61d38d732d4","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:38:49.595359Z","id":"35b8b1427337b5bdcf776f42a01baaecd171c03f6f11364bbc64c202a99592fa","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:503-503, record fced511a.\n\napi_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":596},"end":{"line":596},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","supersedes":"a24163203238c92e139f51f53530274230534c03a23c714b2222331893198641","tags":["people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:38:50.617165Z","id":"8c11a7ecfb9fced95f7c573a50093fd442af799ccf8dc3008d9b85f36ef4b4ed","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:998-998, record 3c0ad45d.\n\nEvery handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1199},"end":{"line":1199},"content_hash":"0084401cde97b2431fc0a50fda577f15da02d5950c956b6bd243c5b7d069ce7d"},"summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"18483473fec681267aa5ae14df64f95a65be784dad0b4ba868d1d8e68721d409","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:38:51.430416Z","id":"8c35f7f60d9c7a4f5e06ee02ea6cf62451699b2dc723b766beda390d0033a3d3","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:197-200, record ed323928.\n\nLimits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":216},"end":{"line":219},"content_hash":"e773e1438242b272aff7abb4426e25b6868af8c1d503cc1f0ab28083fc52603f"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","supersedes":"c2022c63f2969f16db7ca867692e2875bc8c87063d9408a7b7d49f76dac23cd5","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T14:54:56.622382Z","id":"76ece95f3cf0bc09d07fe13fc2eb1096631beee48cb108fef75172c1213f44d2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"75c0506b253ac283a35c6618578644946e0d8b609fd3cf300c2af90ef381043f","summary":"Now no hosted caller holds the gallery topic: member_gate drops Topic::Gallery for every scoped caller (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1119), and the owner's browser and the daemon token are scoped callers too, so the owner's gallery does not update live on a hosted daemon either until the gallery topic is filtered per reach.","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T14:54:56.622505Z","id":"ad14a41434aa84163d0c10d4b315c2b9a58acb36a59a5e3f8bbe0c8b58f71a1e","body":{"detail":"person_allows applies the person's rights (person_rights, shares included) with own resolved by the person, then the link's, as before the reach rule. Asker::Owner and Asker::OwnerAgent in allows_one allow everything. The HTTP routes that mint a git token pass the gate's MemberRights (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs allows_at), but a held token's later checks (recheck) and fork lineage reads go through allows_one, which still reads every artifact for the owner and for a person with clax:collaborator rights.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":326},"end":{"line":347},"content_hash":"0dcd6668040748e4bf2e41c4cd3afc1cb9dd8ed444600242440a27e9d400f659"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted daemon, check Asker::Person with MemberRights::of_person(..).allows_at and Asker::Owner/OwnerAgent with MemberRights::owner(..).allows_at, and Asker::PersonAgent with clax_http::agent::grant_at.","summary":"A person's git asker is not scoped to their reach: their rights' * location reaches another person's artifact through git","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T18:24:54.761349Z","id":"d66e67cd38ab61ea357356f3f6a77c0e9154d90b73ea2855c3e42e8cd3bc7b10","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"75c0506b253ac283a35c6618578644946e0d8b609fd3cf300c2af90ef381043f","summary":"Proposed for resolution (owner's call): since c1f49dfc every hosted caller holds the gallery topic again, scoped to them. crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs (update) maps gallery to Topic::GalleryOf(MemberRights::gallery_key()), and the hub (crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs Hub::check_gallery, gallery_routes) delivers each gallery event of an artifact only where MemberRights::gallery_reads (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs) says the person reads it, plus the artifact_deleted of one that was in their reach. Test: api_hosted::the_gallery_topic_carries_only_what_its_subscriber_reads (crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs) passes under bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__5: the owner's and Mia's galleries update live, the owner hears nothing of Mia's page, both hear a deletion. Unit: stream::tests::a_scoped_gallery_gets_only_events_its_check_admits (//crates/clax-realtime:clax_realtime_lib_test).","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T18:25:05.375109Z","id":"584aa4fbc3da44fbdac8007b7c3d84933c2aa21779e56fdf7d701381bc902551","body":{"detail":"MemberRights::gallery_reads falls back, for a Gone artifact, to the person's granted rights over what the owner or they made; share rights (share_rights_of) and link access cover only live artifacts, so a person who saw a shared or linked page in their gallery keeps its card until they reload after its maker deletes it. Every gallery event of an artifact calls gallery_reads once per Chan::GalleryOf channel (crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs gallery_routes), and each call builds MemberRights (person_rights plus share_rights_of) and runs reach and link_access: several store reads per subscribed person per event, on the publishing thread, as check_reads' reads_now does per reader channel. A per-person scope cache invalidated on rights, share and revocation changes would cut it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":989},"end":{"line":1012},"content_hash":"e8ceae762a0c5de03c348d8f185650d28ed7c4989d7a2e867a9e3744bcf4e55d"},"summary":"A deleted artifact reached only by a share or its link never sends artifact_deleted to that person's scoped gallery, and each gallery event costs a scope build per subscribed gallery","tags":["revisit:scale","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T18:40:16.298368Z","id":"c06eb79fd668a408453bb9cad1830aaf9d6f14a6e01be3fcc9a1c35acd98544f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"584aa4fbc3da44fbdac8007b7c3d84933c2aa21779e56fdf7d701381bc902551","summary":"Since 6341c64e gallery_reads (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs) never admits by link: it runs reach, then granted rights (Within, or Gone for the owner's or the maker's artifact) or share rights (Beyond), with no link_access read. A deleted artifact a person reached only by a share still sends no artifact_deleted to their gallery; one reached by link was never in it.","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T19:34:25.880409Z","id":"4bf3d2bc237eb800a136cb58acc075dfe05e4d2e95cea021c8d235b7e9a550ca","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"63ce5763c0196d3bba5e418b059982564b9fe0d3069fcdf8a0d21bdcd088927e","summary":"Since 4fb02e27, on a hosted daemon, a person's (and the owner's) inbox leaves out items about artifacts out of their reach (crates/clax-http/src/views/inbox.rs out_of_reach, MemberRights::lists: by rights within reach, by share beyond it, never by link) in its lists, groups, counts, one item and the inbox events, and GET /api/viewers/me/attention without ?artifact= holds only artifacts their reach lists (crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs). GET /api/viewers/me/seen needs ?artifact=, which the gate checks. What remains: a local daemon's connected people are not filtered (by design there); a hosted item reached only through a page's link is now left out too, and POST /api/inbox/read {ids} still marks such an item by its ID. Test: api_hosted::no_owner_path_reads_a_members_page.","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T19:34:43.578243Z","id":"f957508a479d219ba5234d3b5b3b19e33a2d509302cdb1e96779c9d5e128b877","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4fb02e27","summary":"Fixed in 4fb02e27: on a hosted daemon allows_one and person_allows hold every asker to their reach (a person and the owner or the owner's agents by MemberRights::allows_at, a person's agent by grant_at), at mint, at recheck and up a fork's lineage, and hosts list the owner's own tokens so a recheck covers them. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__2 prints 'test api_git_tokens::a_share_is_all_that_reaches_another_persons_page_through_git ... ok'; before the fix it failed with Sam's token cxt_1 not revoked when Mia's share ended.","supersedes":"ad14a41434aa84163d0c10d4b315c2b9a58acb36a59a5e3f8bbe0c8b58f71a1e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:23:30.698794Z","id":"bb514c729f0109bb96934c8bdf349e93be46a1e4b6e736ff46f94e0b068f7044","body":{"detail":"Beside the deleted page reached by a share: when a share ends (DELETE /api/hosted/artifacts/<aid>/shares/<id>) or its maker is revoked (DELETE /api/people/<pid>), no event tells the galleries that listed the page, so its card stays until the gallery refetches; and a sharee's gallery never gets artifact_deleted for another person's page. On the cost side, MemberRights::gallery_reads (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1019) builds MemberRights::owner or MemberRights::of_person (person_rights and share_rights_of) and runs Store::reach for every gallery event, once per subscribed Chan::GalleryOf, synchronously on the thread that publishes the event (Hub::check_gallery, crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs).","kind":"comment","references":"584aa4fbc3da44fbdac8007b7c3d84933c2aa21779e56fdf7d701381bc902551","suggested_fix":"Cache the scope per dispatch, or per (gallery key, visibility generation) since every rights, share and revocation change bumps the generation; and on a share's end or a revocation publish an artifact_removed (or artifact_deleted) to the galleries that held the page.","summary":"Two more gaps of the same scoped gallery: no event when a page leaves a gallery's reach, and the scope is built per event per gallery on the publishing thread","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:23:30.699121Z","id":"c72d67d7034f0d09f1197d24489a452c6c49132a87bbfdb7bc568da2991259fa","body":{"detail":"owners_people_view removes from each access object the locations naming artifacts out of the owner's reach and counts them in hidden_locations (tested by api_hosted::the_owners_people_names_no_page_of_another_person). The shell (web/shell/src/people) builds the owner's changes from what it was shown: PUT /api/people/<pid>/rights (crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs set_rights) replaces a person's rights with the value sent, so the owner re-saving a person's rights from People removes the hidden locations from them. Raises are per granter and narrowings are the person's, so only a person's rights round-trip this way; those locations name another person's artifacts, where granted rights have no effect on hosted (the reach rule), so nothing a person may do changes today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1064},"end":{"line":1107},"content_hash":"41294579380e6815f5488408bfbf51e56ec211a988309954a468461835e3bf45"},"suggested_fix":"Have set_rights keep the stored locations out of the owner's reach when it replaces a person's rights on hosted, or refuse a value that would drop them; or leave as is while granted rights at another person's artifact stay inert.","summary":"A rights value People shows the owner on hosted leaves out hidden locations, so an edit built from it drops them","tags":["hosted","people","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:23:42.377149Z","id":"71808ffbd906efd78fff85debaa9834dc5fa9390a75b56d4b0ec631d612be6dd","body":{"detail":"owners_people_view removes from each access object the locations naming artifacts out of the owner's reach and counts them in hidden_locations (tested by api_hosted::the_owners_people_names_no_page_of_another_person). PUT /api/people/<pid>/rights (crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs set_rights) replaces a person's rights with the value sent, and the shell (web/shell/src/people) builds that value from what People showed, so the owner re-saving a person's rights drops the hidden locations. Those include artifact IDs of the person's own pages, which are within the person's reach and do grant there (a location naming another person's artifact has no effect on hosted). Raises are per granter and narrowings are the person's own, so only a person's rights round-trip this way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1064},"end":{"line":1107},"content_hash":"41294579380e6815f5488408bfbf51e56ec211a988309954a468461835e3bf45"},"suggested_fix":"On hosted, have set_rights keep the stored locations out of the owner's reach when it replaces a person's rights (the owner cannot see them, so cannot mean to drop them), or refuse a value that would drop them.","summary":"A rights value People shows the owner on hosted leaves out hidden locations, so an edit built from it drops them","supersedes":"c72d67d7034f0d09f1197d24489a452c6c49132a87bbfdb7bc568da2991259fa","tags":["hosted","people","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:43.884506Z","id":"ad48c381263a84deab7c57beca2a37b871639a1b47c2fc833fb6fa6d2acc70ec","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs:532-543, record 0caf9cae.\n\nAsker::Link has no reader (Asker::reader is None, as for people), so check_history does not run for it: no 503 while pushed commits wait (clax_core::store::pushes), and Store::repo_history's refused_pushers' commits stay reachable from main. A member's clone carries the same, but a link reaches anyone who has it. Narrowing would need a host that serves only version tags to link tokens.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs:313:324 to crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs:340:351: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":340},"end":{"line":351},"content_hash":"0d09c7764a8f34cc69851914496389ab09377c6c3b88d93e1f64ff0a1f6de19e"},"summary":"A page link's read token clones main whole: pushed commits not yet recorded as versions, and refused pushes left on main, reach whoever holds the link, though the page shows them only its versions","supersedes":"86481da4da4869896caa807e0d37b6b17d95fa13dd8531bf8d2b86d11c3ef387","tags":["git","hosted","security","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:43.934913Z","id":"40f09345a6cb698e00d2fbcf862f6854a15c8f7dd057b29570300b9e0d8f6bb6","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs:730-750, record c906a641.\n\nA pasted command lands in the shell's history with the token, and while git runs any user of the machine can read its -c argument in the process list. The GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0/GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 form (what jj_clone_command and the jj commands use) keeps it out of other users' process list but not out of the history, and does not work as pasted in PowerShell or cmd; a credential helper given inline (-c credential.helper=...) is on the command line the same way. Keeping it out of the history needs two steps (read the token into a variable, then run the command with it), which a one-paste flow does not have. docs/contract.md 'Git remotes' states the trade; the tokens' lives (3600 s, 900 s for agents) bound it.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs:511:531 to crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs:563:583: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":563},"end":{"line":583},"content_hash":"6b54dbed5895c129171356cda07b70b28b4862cb13ea6c3e866d6a1beb86530f"},"summary":"The commands carry the token on git's command line (-c http.extraHeader), as the hosted spec's section 9 and hosted/src/git/commands.ts do, not in the environment or a credential helper","supersedes":"98af064f2c7a184426f074a7ff2cd598194dd3b2795ab7e38810ded4cf168dad","tags":["security","revisit:shared multi-user machines are a target, or the dialog grows a two-step flow","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:43.983466Z","id":"9c9266629b74111ad1a3f3ccb77255748accaac34d7586dfaecb361c71e83c84","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:197-200, record ed323928.\n\nLimits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:194:197 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:233:236: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":233},"end":{"line":236},"content_hash":"c3d9cee2df2daa7466bec6f2d7785f46a526e8ffaae9cfc54cec9c2e75b2fe50"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","supersedes":"930a2cdfdfee1ac179d6d28c701931c7cda59a419ca69a2e84bfa48c27d7b68f","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:44.031591Z","id":"2c2d93e0e7a3c9c7d6a510bd640006b32c51c2afb55172c65a52c8990c61665d","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:542-544, record 16ca7740.\n\ncontent_key is an HMAC of <aid>/<n> under the daemon token, as the prototype's commit hash (hosted/src/content.ts) never expired either. A person whose rights narrow, or a guest whose page stops being shared, still reads every version address they were handed (not later versions). A new daemon token changes every key.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:539:541 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:621:623: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":621},"end":{"line":623},"content_hash":"cd8d880448cdb31132019e34c90867877b5c99850f7b334415ffebc58c2ce63d"},"suggested_fix":"Mix a per-artifact generation into the key and bump it when the page stops being shared or a person's rights narrow.","summary":"A content key never expires: whoever saw a version's keyed address keeps reading it after losing the right","supersedes":"ad4d8d8c97b30ea324cdbd7218826481a8ddbad720b28cae710d7325b0f14f3a","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:44.079913Z","id":"499148ea2b97d3bef23e82d9ab0884cbb07d5b3c6d79b3318ab363ee4079b7a8","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:669-674, record 6b80c3e5.\n\nThe gate could require /c/<aid>/draft/k/<content key of the base version>/<agent>/<token>/…, so a draft URL is also bound to a key the daemon derives. Not taken: the draft token is already 128 random bits minted per revision (clax_core::drafts::new_token), handed only to people who may read the artifact, and it expires with the revision, which a content key never does; a second key adds a path segment the shell's draftSrc (web/shell/src/view/draft-model.ts) and the artifact host rewrite (crates/clax-server/src/host.rs) would carry for no capability the token lacks.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:666:671 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:746:751: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":746},"end":{"line":751},"content_hash":"1784c2024ba3d1b89730649afd8e4da2b8bb437c88275427391e1e49fcc54dd8"},"summary":"Draft URLs keyed by the version's content key as well as the draft token","supersedes":"2b006cc0e57d1bd9a98cc8d7e7d29b29e8ed2b344bd59cf97af640eb110821f3","tags":["hosted","drafts","revisit:a draft token is logged, persisted or handed to anyone who may not read the artifact","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:44.128681Z","id":"3b2f25db67107400d1aa65e7ef28cf62c3f440679004eb4bcf92f8a40efa102f","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:933-937, record a625cb63.\n\nmember_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:930:934 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1263:1267: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1263},"end":{"line":1267},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","supersedes":"63ce5763c0196d3bba5e418b059982564b9fe0d3069fcdf8a0d21bdcd088927e","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:44.177804Z","id":"c6e87646245a3e02aee9f6e78937a114c4d4d90a3ac72b03b89f8b79910eae32","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1181-1183, record 5d1ab740.\n\nThe prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1178:1180 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1499:1501: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1499},"end":{"line":1501},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","supersedes":"4f449f18717d16fa8462adf699146a5355235181cab5bd661d6d2cd09923b033","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:44.227571Z","id":"dd08dcf33cb2baf9335ba4bd9b0da404404e4beeb52336e3ad580d4e9a8133f9","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1607-1615, record 5be58509.\n\nPUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1604:1612 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1970:1978: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1970},"end":{"line":1978},"content_hash":"d6db51fbfe5931fb0d00605685ea2de5cccafa046c6c89f623e78fc68fb20aa2"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","supersedes":"ddaee3f9dbacd808b879f2923a80d54cbfe33c1412ad1171fdad9b4e6608e4e6","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:46.036081Z","id":"6ab69f5e9834b310804f2468178a93d070380219b09056fc4ba256cc3ad30cc6","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:998-998, record 3c0ad45d.\n\nEvery handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:1166:1166 to crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:1284:1284: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1284},"end":{"line":1284},"content_hash":"70159c01f5d2722d2fc4945c93216b297a9e269ea1785d2c1539aabdc32321d7"},"summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"18483473fec681267aa5ae14df64f95a65be784dad0b4ba868d1d8e68721d409","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:46.087024Z","id":"c1e499ce5110f63c6f606fa77937ecbcdaf79723ca8a162dc923b3d00d1a8897","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs:948-979, record 27341258.\n\nrecheck asks the host for every live held token (RepoDO token/held on the Worker) and, per token, builds a Visibility and reads Store::repo_history (the artifact's and its lineage's versions and refused pushers). listen runs it after every Version, ArtifactDeleted, People and Agents event burst; settle_layer before answering a request that moved the generation; and listen once when a server is built (each Durable Object wake). Fine for a handful of tokens; with many, a recheck per artifact and a per-reader Visibility cache would bound it.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs:729:760 to crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs:817:849: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":817},"end":{"line":849},"content_hash":"069aad7db7bc0e5e96738ab36cf4da7dcb800ec19f1bf057b07d840c357ddd8b"},"summary":"A recheck lists every held token from the host and walks each one's repository history: run on every relevant event, every request that moves the visibility generation, and every server built anew","supersedes":"6531e06a2d4417884ec020f91d1f78d5f77e0386b9f536c305c91c0e5b617665","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:46.136233Z","id":"9c5cbb8e87bcdf5999ec013f99796eab3473d513add3645812f9d1ec0f3de44f","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:565-591, record 4585fb7a.\n\nThe keyed address is an HMAC of <aid>/<tid> (clip_key), not a hash of the PNG: a thread's clip is written once and never changes for that (artifact, thread) pair (a move to another artifact makes a new pair, crates/clax-core/src/store/site.rs put_clip), so the address is immutable without reading every clip to hash it for a listing. Clips stay stored once per thread (ContentStore::put_clip). The hosted shell still loads clip_url (GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/threads/<tid>/clip, credentialed, Cache-Control private, max-age=3600); thread views carry clip_link only for agents (VisFor::of in crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs). Pointing the shell's <img> at the keyed address would make one cacheable URL for both, and needs browser verification of the hosted shell.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:562:588 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:644:668: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":644},"end":{"line":668},"content_hash":"088272ca3a5d64f436e23082a73f135e24cf3f92181ed8b2d2f98437ed5bb7a0"},"summary":"Key a clip's address by its content hash, and have the hosted shell load clips from it","supersedes":"924f246c3d11dfd9cdf02556bed14c4a9b5b18118a7d4c6c868b5a919429fec2","tags":["hosted","revisit:hosted shell clip loads show in the time-to-usable budget, or a clip's bytes may change for its thread","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:07.518013Z","id":"9590dc3b02705592ffc5f9e19ff47369fb86e057f3a726324062cd21a6aaf35e","body":{"detail":"owners_people_view removes from each access object the locations naming artifacts out of the owner's reach and counts them in hidden_locations (tested by api_hosted::the_owners_people_names_no_page_of_another_person). PUT /api/people/<pid>/rights (crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs set_rights) replaces a person's rights with the value sent, and the shell (web/shell/src/people) builds that value from what People showed, so the owner re-saving a person's rights drops the hidden locations. Those include artifact IDs of the person's own pages, which are within the person's reach and do grant there (a location naming another person's artifact has no effect on hosted). Raises are per granter and narrowings are the person's own, so only a person's rights round-trip this way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1070},"end":{"line":1113},"content_hash":"41294579380e6815f5488408bfbf51e56ec211a988309954a468461835e3bf45"},"suggested_fix":"On hosted, have set_rights keep the stored locations out of the owner's reach when it replaces a person's rights (the owner cannot see them, so cannot mean to drop them), or refuse a value that would drop them.","summary":"A rights value People shows the owner on hosted leaves out hidden locations, so an edit built from it drops them","supersedes":"71808ffbd906efd78fff85debaa9834dc5fa9390a75b56d4b0ec631d612be6dd","tags":["hosted","people","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:07.583589Z","id":"8278c9e2850beb1e122e857a49c27121eee929cccd035e2a84c567a8c65fa415","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:197-200, record ed323928.\n\nLimits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:194:197 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:233:236: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":239},"end":{"line":242},"content_hash":"c3d9cee2df2daa7466bec6f2d7785f46a526e8ffaae9cfc54cec9c2e75b2fe50"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","supersedes":"9c9266629b74111ad1a3f3ccb77255748accaac34d7586dfaecb361c71e83c84","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:07.651161Z","id":"e5499b42c4471ec4cde83df826bf879f8203a8877e4a3338eea41dbc5fbdff71","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:542-544, record 16ca7740.\n\ncontent_key is an HMAC of <aid>/<n> under the daemon token, as the prototype's commit hash (hosted/src/content.ts) never expired either. A person whose rights narrow, or a guest whose page stops being shared, still reads every version address they were handed (not later versions). A new daemon token changes every key.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:539:541 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:621:623: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":627},"end":{"line":629},"content_hash":"cd8d880448cdb31132019e34c90867877b5c99850f7b334415ffebc58c2ce63d"},"suggested_fix":"Mix a per-artifact generation into the key and bump it when the page stops being shared or a person's rights narrow.","summary":"A content key never expires: whoever saw a version's keyed address keeps reading it after losing the right","supersedes":"2c2d93e0e7a3c9c7d6a510bd640006b32c51c2afb55172c65a52c8990c61665d","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:07.716558Z","id":"993b78735ccf5188d4c10dec79d62ed2180b8bfb43ef8dc4da828290fe278871","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:669-674, record 6b80c3e5.\n\nThe gate could require /c/<aid>/draft/k/<content key of the base version>/<agent>/<token>/…, so a draft URL is also bound to a key the daemon derives. Not taken: the draft token is already 128 random bits minted per revision (clax_core::drafts::new_token), handed only to people who may read the artifact, and it expires with the revision, which a content key never does; a second key adds a path segment the shell's draftSrc (web/shell/src/view/draft-model.ts) and the artifact host rewrite (crates/clax-server/src/host.rs) would carry for no capability the token lacks.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:666:671 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:746:751: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":752},"end":{"line":757},"content_hash":"1784c2024ba3d1b89730649afd8e4da2b8bb437c88275427391e1e49fcc54dd8"},"summary":"Draft URLs keyed by the version's content key as well as the draft token","supersedes":"499148ea2b97d3bef23e82d9ab0884cbb07d5b3c6d79b3318ab363ee4079b7a8","tags":["hosted","drafts","revisit:a draft token is logged, persisted or handed to anyone who may not read the artifact","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:07.783084Z","id":"b61447304fa606524cab6f9ba3e192700ba08e4d2c43420c037aaf041beedaa1","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:933-937, record a625cb63.\n\nmember_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:930:934 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1263:1267: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1269},"end":{"line":1273},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","supersedes":"3b2f25db67107400d1aa65e7ef28cf62c3f440679004eb4bcf92f8a40efa102f","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
