{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T16:31:23.866420Z","id":"e57326dd26a914556db43d94e4f88aee07476048756bd2161fb259e46f0edcc4","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 20a84754 (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:650:674): the same record re-anchored on two lines of history (this branch's rebases and main), differing only in the span it cites.","supersedes":"b0159d89c908a1f2da6e9aa8a64a0e5e0db5d4e236e2be189c66329c9cba0b40","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/grant_auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:14:33.626940Z","id":"f633da6c670ae197b92d6c5f6b27cae3aea2a8a8961380140f1b8515a55b6351","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design §5.3 asks for rate limits per reporter_id and per service grant. crates/clax-http/src/limits.rs holds only body caps, and no request limiter exists to reuse. The only bound is the queue nonce cache: QUEUE_NONCES_PER_KEY (1024 signed requests per key per 240 s window, then 429 limit_reached) and QUEUE_KEYS (16384 keys across every queue). A deployer's backend can mint a fresh reporter key per request, so neither cap bounds one reporter_id or one grant; and one queue's reporters can fill QUEUE_KEYS, refusing every other queue's reporters with 429 until their nonces age out.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":479},"end":{"line":490},"content_hash":"42495ede7d680bd724f40f3ddad60135ac17a9268c644fe7d3295122a7bcbd5d"},"suggested_fix":"Add a per-(queue, reporter_id) and per-service-grant token bucket in clax-http (injected clock), checked in ServiceCaller/ReporterCaller after the token lookup, and give each queue its own share of the key cap.","summary":"A queue's service and reporter routes have no rate limit per reporter_id or per service grant, only a nonce cap per signing key","tags":["security","hosted","queues","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/grant_auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:24:00.334516Z","id":"5e9c8e8be0fba83dcbd795f251bc278324a62c03d16f6343bb3840b14c861f8f","body":{"detail":"head() reads header::HOST as received; the signer (web/sdk/src/sign.ts, crates/clax-core/src/sig.rs) signs the host it sent to. A Kubernetes ingress or other proxy that forwards with its own Host (for example an upstream service name) makes every grant, service and reporter request answer 401 invalid_signature. A deployment must preserve Host (nginx proxy_set_header Host $host; most ingresses do by default), or the daemon must be told its public host. docs/ has no deployment note saying so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":786},"end":{"line":791},"content_hash":"4d0b883080ecbccae4cb839850652c733221076b55d09370ba8747d0a4ccec86"},"summary":"A signed request verifies against the Host header the daemon receives, so a reverse proxy or ingress that rewrites Host breaks every signature","tags":["queues","deploy","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/reporter.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T15:38:04.587468Z","id":"5787d6d49e47769b3f04d014ef5f36850e7e5274acd6449d4f545dff4eb9a15f","body":{"detail":"Browsers send no `Origin` on a same-origin GET, so the instance's own pages (clax.dev's shell, web/shell/src/feedback/) could not read the badge or their reports (403 wrong_origin, seen in web/e2e/feedback.spec.ts before this rule). `same_origin_as` compares only the Host's authority with the token origin's, so an http page on the same host and port would pass for an https token (one listener serves one scheme, so this needs a proxy serving both). Browsers that send no Sec-Fetch-Site (Safari before 16.4) still get 403 on these reads. Test: crates/clax-server/tests/api_queue_reporter.rs a_same_origin_read_without_origin_holds_only_on_the_tokens_host.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"10ceb979e3776d2cbade7952820f692d0ce6c85a994719f8602e4fc4fa971a95"},"suggested_fix":"Compare the scheme too where the daemon knows it (its public origin when hosted, else browser_base), or have the SDK send reads as POST so the browser adds Origin.","summary":"A reporter request with no Origin is taken as from the token's origin on Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin and a matching Host; the scheme is not compared, and browsers without Sec-Fetch-Site cannot read","tags":["review","security","feedback-loop","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/reporter.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T16:11:42.076634Z","id":"bb0391c8d48cc4f86019817c0c1fdc641df2dbac28dfb63e089d644c3ecae103","body":{"detail":"`same_origin_as` takes a reporter request with no `Origin` as the token origin's only for a GET or HEAD with one `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin`, one `Host` equal to the token origin's host and port, and the token origin's scheme equal to the instance's public origin's (crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs public_origin). Safari before 16.4 sends no Sec-Fetch-Site, so on an instance that is its own product (clax.dev's shell) its badge and 'Your reports' reads get 403 wrong_origin there; filing (a POST, which carries Origin) works. Tests: the unit test a_same_origin_read_needs_get_or_head_one_mark_one_host_and_the_scheme and crates/clax-server/tests/api_queue_reporter.rs a_same_origin_read_without_origin_holds_only_on_the_tokens_host.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":102},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"3650d3dda2df4312593339207f600fad660198679cd738ccbf5231fb63c48086"},"suggested_fix":"If old Safari matters, have the SDK send its reporter reads as POST (which carries Origin), or accept a matching Referer when Sec-Fetch-Site is absent.","summary":"A browser that sends no Sec-Fetch-Site cannot read reporter routes from the instance's own pages","supersedes":"5787d6d49e47769b3f04d014ef5f36850e7e5274acd6449d4f545dff4eb9a15f","tags":["review","feedback-loop","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:16.401505Z","id":"27d5c161093afbd6aa442fb1ddaa97600f518e3eda251ae6e35ce0601f70761c","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:503-503, record fced511a.\n\napi_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":695},"end":{"line":695},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","supersedes":"35b8b1427337b5bdcf776f42a01baaecd171c03f6f11364bbc64c202a99592fa","tags":["people","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:16.491188Z","id":"1e61aa81a07ad343fad15075cb419372ba1aa39b7544591fa03871fd1d5bb4fa","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:998-998, record 3c0ad45d.\n\nEvery handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:1166:1166 to crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:1284:1284: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1426},"end":{"line":1426},"content_hash":"70159c01f5d2722d2fc4945c93216b297a9e269ea1785d2c1539aabdc32321d7"},"summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"b957fff428e8d307c88c895c51614fd47a53019a70c48fb96a14273182f52221","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:16.584155Z","id":"ddf89bd9c3f0154382f6b4a50e4fa7fa6e80fd53ded5cf9c63574268dfb2f799","body":{"detail":"verify_bearer hands a person-device grant a PersonDevice whose who is the person's member session (Store::person_device_viewer), and crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs browser_or_device takes it as that session: may_share and session_reads read the person's rights, never the grant's narrowing. Narrowing applies to a grant's sessions (Store::grant_caller); the Clax app's token opens none on these routes. A person who narrows the app's token on People still lets it share every artifact they made.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2298},"end":{"line":2319},"content_hash":"ac6260549d2bff9f04aa3a9c74651b357e21dee778ee91f1b320200da366acc8"},"suggested_fix":"Intersect with Store::grant_caller(gid, None)'s rights in person_device_viewer's caller, or hide Narrow for kind device on People.","summary":"A person's device acts on sharing with its person's full rights: narrowing its grant (PUT /api/people/me/grants/<gid>/narrow) does not limit it","supersedes":"f2415df240c8904293bf1bbb53ee8d6de293bbe39bdcb552c6fd38d3d9eaba25","tags":["security","app-push","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:16.683635Z","id":"c37a7da6d3af6ef40a8d22da3300265fdb7548d629004efd3dc33411c75d9853","body":{"detail":"MovingAppData::copies_once runs once per artifact per process; the state read (Store::app_data_state) is a separate store hop from the route's own (Decided in crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs), since the host behind AppDataHost::call takes only the artifact and the operation. Passing the state in would need the trait to take it.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":266},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"1705fce1d2402451810da4c4e925df5d2d4417d0a6de0fe1f39ba8b682a55bbf"},"summary":"Every artifact's first call after a start makes an extra AuditSince call to make up lost audit copies, and every db call still makes its own instance read of the artifact's move state","supersedes":"60abbf154dcc5a4097759b061a99feff19928fe4f3b01caad7ebf94a6ef26799","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:16.781904Z","id":"7609e81c1a81ca3b33ac7a7a7ee67b34bf42c73d6662738a38ff934e994f8e79","body":{"detail":"axum 0.8.9 src/serve/listener.rs:30-37 loops 'match Self::accept(self).await { Ok(tup) => return tup, Err(e) => handle_accept_error(e).await }'. handle_accept_error (:140-158) returns at once when is_connection_error (:160-167: ConnectionRefused, ConnectionAborted, ConnectionReset), else logs 'error!(\"accept error: {e}\")' and runs 'tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_secs(1)).await'. So a listener the OS has reclaimed (iOS may close a suspended app's sockets) costs one error log line a second and never ends serve: the daemon keeps running on a dead socket until its host notices (a failing /healthz) and stops and restarts it. Checked against the axum 0.8.9 source crate_universe fetched (Cargo.lock pins axum 0.8.9).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":454},"end":{"line":458},"content_hash":"8ed331101280a14d1d68691a00f18a00232b6e51e8a7fc0d11160a1249d21299"},"summary":"TunedListener::accept never returns an accept error: axum 0.8.9's Listener for TcpListener retries every one, at once for a per-connection error and after a 1 s sleep for any other","supersedes":"a901b7b806a523eb647a2a1e62610efbb8b1eb878cdcc583f9bb97589a99235a","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:16.875491Z","id":"916e3bfa6f0d32c603eb27084f0ef5f2657c3f747a634f5b1b8513c10f3f22df","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1181-1183, record 5d1ab740.\n\nThe prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1178:1180 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1499:1501: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1364},"end":{"line":1366},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","supersedes":"9ddc9cd4c117c62ef3ce99e56f68a6a80de8ee159178ef8d473b9bce992beb50","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:16.975242Z","id":"bc555b1cc98a1739a4bc610d22d0ff3061c42cc468eb85e7bbcb7b7e44e305ee","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1607-1615, record 5be58509.\n\nPUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1604:1612 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1970:1978: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1850},"end":{"line":1858},"content_hash":"d6db51fbfe5931fb0d00605685ea2de5cccafa046c6c89f623e78fc68fb20aa2"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","supersedes":"a479d008261feb72aa0030afe8b0fd4dc7117f2008c5617d3b11588cf815c7cf","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:17.068578Z","id":"97a1734026f17e248f45cb735095fc72c1d27521e8554689ada45e4ccbc10a32","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs:496-503, record f3b6a110.\n\nIdentity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":730},"end":{"line":737},"content_hash":"e518245782ac10f00f2b65f20d7c675055af73af8c7fb3c52ec0df3ab6eb723b"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"c77c0394c086d807772f6441102c3ff94e064baf6b44658b4202fd6529dfe544","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:49.438396Z","id":"30d9e72bc5a98ee49d074706fb7a22e710ad66f8b811f08288901f6b6adb7bdf","body":{"detail":"A cache of open stores would save it, but the artifact's delete (FsContent::delete_artifact removing artifacts/<id>/) would then have to close the cached connection first.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"02b6f8b33eeb50dd44d00b3872933533a7141910f1e11a3b133c40e5f26e9096"},"summary":"LocalAppData opens the artifact's data.sqlite on every call: a connection and its WAL setup per db operation","supersedes":"38ee5f21ab1b56c2088b6d9661fddb207ec1f0d2181086a7b81913f89c7ff050","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:49.543072Z","id":"b837692dbfa0d96ab3ff3cfb9135afa677eec8bac0d6b725a55071a60bdb70b4","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/extension.rs:219-225, record e63a6a28.\n\nAdmitting /api/questions and /api/inbox for the extension credential with Rule::Any widens the extension's live-only posture (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-05-chrome-overlay-design.md section 9.5). docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:902-915 lists what it lets the extension see and states this is an open owner question. Decision needed: keep this, or restore the live-only posture by filtering /api/inbox and /api/questions to live-page items for the extension, leaving out other items' artifact, and refusing the item and question routes for items that are not live.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068)'s record.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":219},"end":{"line":227},"content_hash":"f594c2aa4e21cbea1698593a51129d543a3032dfe96aa589e2c0b6bc55f8707a"},"summary":"The extension, acting as the owner, may list and read every inbox item and question, gallery artifacts' included","supersedes":"d5b8f79e902a51fb14ffb501f131430e3f7a3c20bc1cd0dc11771b67087e965c","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:49.650603Z","id":"2a98e452464444535d9ebb0ed5ba3a9aaf821f587bed610c4d75b2a3196bfa05","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs:28-31, record 0bcf4f58.\n\nA LAN viewer (the clax_viewer cookie) can create viewers, threads, comments, sends and db documents without limit. Decision needed: add rate limits for LAN writes, and at what rates.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"45d95b0d3096f1a7c098ddac445238243c2cee229e789f6b6501a7e351453518"},"summary":"LAN viewers' writes have no rate limit","supersedes":"0a1a0d4b04504252c8f9703038c055b7e0ee47f052ebc29bf8a1458c77a32cd3","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/reporter.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:20:51.413649Z","id":"93cfd4044fc34ec491b2c0bd8b1efc5199f349fa561872afba2a6d1cb79a3740","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"bb0391c8d48cc4f86019817c0c1fdc641df2dbac28dfb63e089d644c3ecae103","summary":"On the Worker too: crates/clax-worker/test-feedback.mjs (commit 103c91c06) checks that a reporter badge or list read with neither Origin nor Sec-Fetch-Site is 403 wrong_origin under wrangler dev, while the same read with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin and the public Host is 200. The concern stands as written.","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
